{#
    The toolbox declaration widget (SPEC §4.1, §15), as a macro — shared by
    the task's own declaration, every step's, and a conversation's, because
    they are the same declaration at different scopes and in different
    places. Import with:

        {% import '_toolbox.html.twig' as toolbox_ui %}

    Lives at the template root rather than under `task/` for that reason: it
    is no longer only the task editor's widget. A chat is the third caller,
    and the reason it is one macro and not three is the same either way —
    the field names it posts are the contract the parser reads
    (`App\Admin\ToolboxSelection`), so a second copy of this markup would be
    a second chance to post something the parser does not understand.

    Two pickers, one active: `tags` resolves against the discovered catalog
    (task.tags ∩ tool.tags), `explicit` names tools exactly. The inactive
    picker is hidden by the editor script but stays in the DOM, so a mode
    switch never loses what was typed — and the server honours only the
    selected mode's list (TaskEditorSubmission), so the hidden one cannot leak
    into the saved declaration.

    Alongside each checkbox list is a free-text companion: the catalog is
    discovered, not authoritative, so a human must be able to declare a tool
    or tag it does not carry yet. The detail page's preview is what tells them
    when such a declaration resolves to nothing. It is seeded with the
    declared entries the catalog does not offer as a checkbox — otherwise
    reopening and re-saving a task would silently drop them.

    `prefix` is the field-name scope: '' for the task's own declaration
    (top-level field names, `toolbox_mode` — the parser reads the task's
    scalars flat, so the toolbox has to match), 'steps[l][s]' for a step's.

    The checkbox arrays need their empty-bracket suffix OUTSIDE the prefix's
    closing bracket — `steps[0][0][toolbox_tags][]`, never
    `steps[0][0][toolbox_tags[]]`. The latter is not a PHP array at all: the
    parser keeps `toolbox_tags[` as a literal key, so every checked box is
    silently discarded and only the free-text companion survives the save.

    Each free-text companion is seeded only from the declaration that belongs
    to *its own* mode: a tags declaration seeds "More tags" (with the entries
    the catalog does not carry), an explicit declaration seeds "More tools" —
    and never the other way round. Seeding both from the same stored list is
    how a tags task used to arrive with its tags pasted into the tool-name
    field, ready to be saved as tool names by an accidental mode switch.

    ## `collapsed` — the picker behind a disclosure

    `collapsed` wraps the whole picker in a `<details>` and **defaults to
    false**, so this is a no-op for every caller that does not ask for it (the
    task editor still shows the picker flat, because there the picker *is* the
    point of the page). The two chat pages ask for it: there the picker is a
    permission panel sitting between the box you type in and the Send button,
    and a screenful of tool vocabulary you did not come to read is the one
    thing in the way of the conversation.

    Folding it hides the *choosing*, not the answer. The summary states the
    current declaration, and the declaration itself travels in hidden inputs
    inside the `<details>` — read the block below the summary before changing
    either, because "the summary is a report and the inputs are the answer" is
    the whole reason this is safe.

    `open` is deliberately absent: nothing remembers that it was open, and a
    server-side default of "open" would un-collapse it for everyone. That also
    decides where the `errors[group]` message goes — it is rendered *outside*
    the `<details>`, as a sibling, so a refused submission can never slide its
    complaint into a shut drawer and leave the page looking as though it
    silently did nothing. (The chat pages do not populate `errors` at all; the
    task editor does, and does not collapse, so this holds for both.)
#}
{% macro toolbox(prefix, values, tags, tools, errors, group, disabled = false, collapsed = false) %}
{% if collapsed %}
{#
    The summary is what makes a collapsed picker usable: without it, shutting
    the drawer would hide the answer to "what can she do right now?", which is
    the property the whole permission surface was designed around.

    The names come from copies taken here rather than from the `{% set %}`s
    further down. Twig scopes a `set` to the body of the block it appears in,
    and those assignments sit at macro scope *after* this branch — so reading
    them here would be reading a variable that does not exist yet (and trips
    `strict_variables`, which the test environment turns on). `values` and
    `errors` are arguments, so they are in scope, and neither is `|default`ed
    on purpose: a default would silently paper over a caller that forgot one.

    Only the ACTIVE mode's list is reported. The inactive one is an artefact
    of keeping both panels in the DOM, not part of the answer, and
    `ToolboxSelection` does not read it — the summary says what was chosen,
    not what is lying around.
#}
{% set summary_mode = values.toolbox_mode|default('tags') %}
{% set summary_declared = values.toolbox|default([]) %}
{% set summary_is_tag = summary_mode == 'tags' %}
{% set summary_catalog_names = tools|map(t => t.name) %}
{# A declaration the catalog no longer carries still counts as declared. #}
{% set summary_known = summary_is_tag
    ? summary_declared|filter(v => v in tags)
    : summary_declared|filter(v => v in summary_catalog_names) %}
{% set summary_unknown = summary_is_tag
    ? summary_declared|filter(v => v not in tags)
    : summary_declared|filter(v => v not in summary_catalog_names) %}
{# Known first, then the ones the catalog has dropped; at most three, then a count. #}
{% set summary_all = summary_known|merge(summary_unknown) %}
{% set summary_shown = summary_all|length > 3 ? summary_all|slice(0, 3) : summary_all %}
<details class="toolbox-disclosure">
    <summary>
        Toolbox
        <span class="muted">{{ summary_is_tag ? 'by tag' : 'by name' }}</span>
        {% if summary_shown is empty %}
            <span class="muted">— none</span>
        {% else %}
            <span class="tool-set">·</span>
            {% for entry in summary_shown %}<code>{{ entry }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="tool-set">·</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
            {% if summary_all|length > 3 %}<span class="muted">+{{ summary_all|length - 3 }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% endif %}
    </summary>

    {#
        The hidden inputs below carry the declaration while the drawer is shut,
        and this is the comment to read before touching them.

        A `disabled` control is not submitted at all. The chat passes
        `disabled` while a reply is pending, and it *opens* the drawer in that
        state — so without these, saving that page would submit no mode and no
        declaration, and the picker would reopen on its defaults rather than on
        the toolbox she is actually running with.

        Only the two array-valued fields appear here. `mode` is flat, so the
        last one wins — which is correct: it is the same value the radios carry
        — but the free-text companions are flat too, and emitting one entry per
        unknown tag would collapse them to whichever came last and silently
        truncate a declaration the catalog does not carry. Those are already
        carried by the fieldset's own text inputs, seeded with exactly the
        entries the catalog does not offer as a checkbox, so they are left
        alone here.

        The values match the boxes they twin: a tag that IS in the catalog goes
        to the checkbox array, and one that is not goes to the companion — the
        same split the fieldset makes, so `ToolboxSelection` reads a submission
        that is identical whether the drawer was open or shut. A checked box
        and its twin submit the same value under an array name, and the parser
        collapses duplicates by key, so the declaration survives the round trip
        unchanged.

        They are omitted when `disabled`, and only for the reason the contents
        below are: a page with no enabled control has no submission to carry
        anything into. That is the chat's pending state and nothing else — the
        task editor's `disabled` (an immutable, already-run task) is never
        collapsed — so the pair of guards describe the same situation rather
        than two different ones.
    #}
    {% if not disabled %}
        <input type="hidden" name="{{ prefix }}toolbox_mode" value="{{ summary_is_tag ? 'tags' : 'explicit' }}">
        {% for entry in summary_known %}<input type="hidden" name="{{ prefix }}{{ summary_is_tag ? 'toolbox_tags' : 'toolbox_tools' }}[]" value="{{ entry }}">{% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% set open = prefix == '' ? '' : prefix ~ '[' %}
{% set close = prefix == '' ? '' : ']' %}
{% set name_mode = open ~ 'toolbox_mode' ~ close %}
{% set name_tags = open ~ 'toolbox_tags' ~ close ~ '[]' %}
{% set name_tags_extra = open ~ 'toolbox_tags_extra' ~ close %}
{% set name_tools = open ~ 'toolbox_tools' ~ close ~ '[]' %}
{% set name_tools_extra = open ~ 'toolbox_tools_extra' ~ close %}
{% set mode = values.toolbox_mode|default('tags') %}
{% set declared = values.toolbox|default([]) %}
{# Each panel is seeded only from a declaration in *its own* mode. #}
{% set tag_selection = mode == 'tags' ? declared : [] %}
{% set tool_selection = mode == 'explicit' ? declared : [] %}
{% set unknown = mode == 'tags' ? declared|filter(v => v not in tags) : [] %}
{% set unknown_tools = mode == 'explicit' ? declared|filter(v => v not in tools|map(t => t.name)) : [] %}
<fieldset class="toolbox">
    <legend>Toolbox</legend>

    <div class="radio-row" role="radiogroup" aria-label="How the toolbox is resolved">
        <label class="radio">
            <input type="radio" name="{{ name_mode }}" value="tags"
                   data-toolbox-mode {{ mode == 'tags' ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
            <span>By tag <span class="muted">— the catalog's tools carrying these tags</span></span>
        </label>
        <label class="radio">
            <input type="radio" name="{{ name_mode }}" value="explicit"
                   data-toolbox-mode {{ mode == 'explicit' ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
            <span>Explicit tools <span class="muted">— exactly these, by name</span></span>
        </label>
    </div>

    <div class="toolbox-panel" data-toolbox-panel="tags" {% if mode != 'tags' %}hidden{% endif %}>
        {% if tags is empty %}
            <p class="muted">No tags in the catalog yet — tag tools on the <a href="{{ path('app_tool_list') }}">tool catalog</a> page, or type tags below.</p>
        {% else %}
            <ul class="check-list">
                {% for tag in tags %}
                    <li>
                        <label class="check">
                            <input type="checkbox" name="{{ name_tags }}" value="{{ tag }}"
                                   {{ tag in tag_selection ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
                            <span><code>{{ tag }}</code></span>
                        </label>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
        <label class="field">
            <span>More tags <span class="muted">(comma-separated; for tags the catalog does not carry yet)</span></span>
            <input type="text" name="{{ name_tags_extra }}" value="{{ unknown|join(', ') }}" autocomplete="off"
                   placeholder="e.g. weather, calendar" {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
        </label>
    </div>

    <div class="toolbox-panel" data-toolbox-panel="explicit" {% if mode != 'explicit' %}hidden{% endif %}>
        {% if tools is empty %}
            <p class="muted">No tools in the catalog yet — register a server and sync on the <a href="{{ path('app_tool_list') }}">tool catalog</a> page, or type tool names below.</p>
        {% else %}
            <ul class="check-list">
                {% for tool in tools %}
                    <li>
                        <label class="check">
                            <input type="checkbox" name="{{ name_tools }}" value="{{ tool.name }}"
                                   {{ tool.name in tool_selection ? 'checked' }} {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
                            <span>
                                <code>{{ tool.server.name }}.{{ tool.name }}</code>
                                {% if tool.hasSideEffect %}<span class="muted"> · side effects</span>{% endif %}
                            </span>
                        </label>
                    </li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
        {% endif %}
        <label class="field">
            <span>More tools <span class="muted">(comma-separated tool names)</span></span>
            <input type="text" name="{{ name_tools_extra }}" value="{{ unknown_tools|join(', ') }}" autocomplete="off"
                   placeholder="e.g. get_weather" {{ disabled ? 'disabled' }}>
        </label>
    </div>

    {% if errors[group] is defined %}
        <p class="field-error" role="alert">{{ errors[group] }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</fieldset>
{% if collapsed %}
</details>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
